# HP39gs stock launch through the original APLET UI and serial disk.
# The stock ROM mounts the host directory over Kermit, reads HP39DIR.*, then
# lazily fetches the selected aplet and library when ENTER launches it.
2000 tap f6
4000 tap f6

# HP39 matrix aliases:
#   G/H/I -> SYMB/PLOT/NUM
#   J/K/L -> HOME/APLET/VIEWS
7000 tap aplet
8000 capture aplet-library
9000 tap f5
10000 capture receive-menu

# HP39/40 2.22 RECEIVE FROM order:
#   HP39 (IrDA), HP39/40 (USB), HP39/40 (Ser),
#   USB Disk drive, Ser. Disk drive.
10500 tap down
11200 tap down
11900 tap down
12600 tap down
12900 capture receive-serial-disk
13300 tap enter

# Directory metadata loads first. This ENTER starts the selected aplet's lazy
# HPGCC000/LIB275L fetch; host-gate then waits for Kermit to report successful
# EOF for LIB275L, which implies both lazy files are complete.
31000 capture remote-aplet
32500 tap enter
34000 capture lazy-fetch
35000 host-gate

# Times below are relative to host-gate release, not emulator start. Kermit EOF
# proves the bytes have arrived, but Stock can still be committing the fetched
# aplet/library or unwinding the serial-disk UI. Retry ENTER sparsely instead
# of guessing a fixed post-transfer delay. Once HPC1 reaches KBRD the harness
# cancels pending launch-only retries, so they cannot contaminate the strict
# payload keyboard progression while ordinary sequence keys remain available.
0 monitor 90000
500 capture fetch-complete
1000 retry enter
11000 retry enter
21000 retry enter
31000 retry enter
46000 retry enter
61000 retry enter
